@@ ============================================================
@@ RTPlanOpp — best Venus-flyby Mars→Earth return over a Mars-departure window
@@ Two-stage search (coarse grid → local refine) over (t3, Venus flyby, Earth arrival),
@@ minimising a combined cost  P = matchErr + 0.1·max(0, turnReq − turnMax)  so it
@@ favours a ballistic (matchErr→0) AND turn-feasible (turnReq ≤ turnMax) swing-by.
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@
@@ Input  : t3lo t3hi   ( t3lo t3hi -- { t3 tv t4 ΔVTEI matchErr turnReq turnMax tof } )
@@   t3lo t3hi : Mars-departure search window (JD). Keep it narrow (~60 d).
@@ Output : the best return itinerary. Feasible ⇔ matchErr≈0 AND turnReq ≤ turnMax.
@@ VALIDATION (device-confirmed): 2459920 2459980 RTPlanOpp ->
@@   { 2459930 2460150 2460220  5.90 0.00084 30.93° 49.72° 290 }  (Mars dep 2022-12-16,
@@   Venus 2023-07-24, Earth 2023-10-02; near-ballistic matchErr<1 m/s, turnReq ≤ turnMax ✓).
@@ Each itinerary joins two legs: Mars → Venus depends on (t3, tv) only, Venus →
@@ Earth on (tv, t4) only. Each leg is computed once and kept, then the 343
@@ points of the refinement only combine them: 98 Lambert solutions instead of
@@ 686, and the same result to the last digit, about six times faster.
@@ ============================================================
 → t3lo t3hi
 « 'Precision' RCL 'HardwareFloatingPoint' RCL → savP savH « HFP 15 Precision DEG
   @ The two legs of an itinerary, each computed once per pair of dates:
   @ Mars → Venus depends on (t3, tv) only, Venus → Earth on (tv, t4) only.
   @ The penalty then combines them as OppRoute does, in the same order.
   @ These programs are kept in locals: they must name no other local.
   @ ( t3 tv -- { viVi tMax } )
   « → a3 av
     « a3 Ⓛ♂Pf  av Ⓛ♀Pf  av a3 -  0.00029591220828559 ⓁLambertU 2 GET  av 'Ⓛ♀Pf' ⓁVΦf -
       → vi « vi
              vi DUP DOT √ 1731.4568 · 1_km/s ·   6351.8 1_km ·   ⒸGM♀  ⓁGAssist  1 GET Uval
              2 →List » » »
   @ ( tv t4 -- viVo )
   « → bv b4 « bv Ⓛ♀Pf  b4 Ⓛ♁Pf  b4 bv -  0.00029591220828559 ⓁLambertU 1 GET  bv 'Ⓛ♀Pf' ⓁVΦf - » »
   @ ( { viVi tMax } viVo -- P )
   « → l1 vo
     « l1 1 GET l1 2 GET → vi tmx
       « vi DUP DOT √  vo DUP DOT √  -  ABS  1731.4568 ·
         vi vo DOT  vi DUP DOT √  vo DUP DOT √  ·  /  ACOS Uval
         tmx - 0 MAX 0.1 · + » » »
   1000000 0 0 0
   → leg1 leg2 pen zzP zzt3 zztv zzt4
   «
     @ Coarse grid, in the order of the former loops
     t3lo t3hi FOR t3
       130 290 FOR d1
         t3 t3 d1 + leg1
         → L1
         « 60 200 FOR d2
             L1  t3 d1 +  t3 d1 + d2 +  leg2  pen
             → P « P zzP < « P 'zzP' STO  t3 'zzt3' STO  t3 d1 + 'zztv' STO  t3 d1 + d2 + 'zzt4' STO » IFT »
           35 STEP »
       40 STEP
     25 STEP
     @ Refinement, ±15 days by 5 around the coarse best: the 49 legs
     @ Venus → Earth first, then for each (t3, tv) its leg Mars → Venus
     zzt3 zztv zzt4
     → b3 bv b4
     « { }
       bv 15 - bv 15 + FOR tv
         b4 15 - b4 15 + FOR t4
           tv t4 leg2 1 →List +
         5 STEP
       5 STEP
       → L2s
       « b3 15 - b3 15 + FOR t3
           0 bv 15 - bv 15 + FOR tv
             1 +
             t3 tv leg1
             → iv L1
             « 0 b4 15 - b4 15 + FOR t4
                 1 +
                 → it
                 « L1  L2s iv 1 - 7 * it + GET  pen
                   → P « P zzP < « P 'zzP' STO  t3 'zzt3' STO  tv 'zztv' STO  t4 'zzt4' STO » IFT »
                   it »
               5 STEP DROP
               iv »
           5 STEP DROP
         5 STEP
       »
     »
     zzt3 zztv zzt4 3 →List   zzt3 zztv zzt4 ⓁOppRoute  +
   »
   savP Precision  IF savH THEN HFP ELSE SFP END »
 »
»
